## Code Review

Full skill definition: `.cursor/rules/skills/code-review/SKILL.md`

### Two-Stage Review

**Stage 1: Spec Compliance**
Check each Product-Spec.md requirement item by item:
- Every feature listed in the Spec must have corresponding code implementation
- UI consistency check (if design mockups exist, verify pixel accuracy)
- All states covered: loading, empty, error, edge cases
- If Stage 1 fails → dispatch feedback-observer with `review_stage1_fail` → re-implement → re-review from Stage 1

**Stage 2: Code Quality**
- Naming conventions (PascalCase/camelCase/kebab-case)
- TypeScript strict mode, no `any`
- Files under 300 lines, single responsibility
- No hardcoded secrets, no dangerous functions (eval, innerHTML)
- No Spec drift (code features not in Product Spec)
- Regression check: existing features not broken
- If Stage 2 fails → dispatch feedback-observer with `review_stage2_fail` → bug-fixer fix → re-review from Stage 1

### Output Format
- ✅ Fully implemented (with code location)
- ⚠️ Partially implemented (with missing details)
- ❌ Not implemented (with Spec reference)
- 🔴 Security issue (with file + line number)
